# `Rust` code example

It is assumed that you have a recent version of `Rust` and its `cargo` package manager installed.
The generated code has a dependency on the [rust-rdkafka](https://crates.io/crates/rdkafka) crate.

To run the examples we first use `cargo build` to build the executables. This will take a few minutes due to
the dependency on `rdkafka`, which depends on `openssl`. The executables will be written to the
`target/debug` directory.

```shell
> cd {{proxy-name}}-example-rust
> cargo build
```

Now we are able to run the executables. First we will list all Kafka topics that we have
read access to.

```shell
> target/debug/list-topics
...
scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}
...
```

Then we will send messages to a Kafka topic. In the example below we use topic
`scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}`. Use `ctrl-c` to stop the program.

```shell
> target/debug/producer scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}
{{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047895
{{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047896
{{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047897
{{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047898
^C
```

Next we will consume records from the same topic. Again, use `ctrl-c` to stop the program.

```shell
> target/debug/consumer scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}
0:2808 {{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047895
0:2809 {{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047896
0:2810 {{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047897
0:2811 {{proxy-name}}-producer-rust: 1780047898
^C
```
